<title>UK: OPEC quota committee may meet Sept 25 - officials.</title>
<headline>OPEC quota committee may meet Sept 25 - officials.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The next meeting of OPEC's quota compliance committee may be on September 25 in Vienna but a final date has not yet been determined, an OPEC official said.</p>
<p>The official said the meeting of the board, comprising the oil ministers of Iran, Libya and Nigeria and OPEC Secretary General Rilwanu Lukman, was scheduled for this month when OPEC ministers last met in June.</p>
<p>He said the meeting will be &quot;routine&quot; and that the members will compare the official production figures provided by the 11 OPEC member states and compare them with estimates compiled by four selected independent sources including Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;There is nothing special to this meeting. It had been on the cards since June. No big outcome will be expected,&quot; the official said. -- Karen Matusic, London newsroom, +44 171 542 6280</p>
</text>
